WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.650
Once again Zann found himself plummeting through a shadowy kaleidoscope of colors and shapes.

2
00:00:06.651 --> 00:00:10.868
This time, though, Wyssa wasn't there to steady or guide him.

3
00:00:10.869 --> 00:00:15.017
As he felt Perda's hand slipping from his arm, he panicked.

4
00:00:15.018 --> 00:00:21.397
Then he realized the magical shackles were still in place, binding him and Perda together.

5
00:00:21.398 --> 00:00:26.059
"Is everyone still here?" he shouted, struggling to look back.

6
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.151
The movement sent him flying in a new direction.

7
00:00:29.152 --> 00:00:32.158
But he could see his friends strung out behind him.

8
00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:37.100
Perda and Gliss were clinging to each other, while Darb hung onto Gliss' legs.

9
00:00:37.101 --> 00:00:42.451
Zing was clutching Zann's backpack with his claws. Everyone looked terrified.

10
00:00:42.452 --> 00:00:45.745
Zann tried to gather his thoughts. It wasn't easy.

11
00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:53.154
His trip through the vortex with Wyssa had been overwhelming enough. This was much, much worse.

12
00:00:53.155 --> 00:00:58.561
Countless wormholes slid past, offering glimpses into other worlds.

13
00:00:58.562 --> 00:01:03.586
How had Wyssa pulled them through one of them? Zann struggled to remember.

14
00:01:03.587 --> 00:01:09.223
"Zann!" Darb's voice sounded faint and frightened. "What do we do now?"

15
00:01:09.224 --> 00:01:14.962
Zann lunged for the next wormhole they passed. His friends were counting on him.

16
00:01:14.963 --> 00:01:18.671
"Oof!" His fingers grasped only empty air.

17
00:01:18.672 --> 00:01:23.162
The effort sent the entire group spinning. Gliss let out a shriek.

18
00:01:23.163 --> 00:01:25.492
"Hold on!" Darb shouted.

19
00:01:25.493 --> 00:01:33.939
"Is everyone okay?" Zann yelled. He could feel Perda's arm shackled to his, and Zing's hot breath on his neck.

20
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.239
Were the other two still with them?

21
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:43.745
"We're okay!" Gliss sounded breathless. "I—I don't know how much longer we can hold on though!"

22
00:01:43.746 --> 00:01:46.714
Zann gulped. He had to get them out of here!

23
00:01:46.715 --> 00:01:51.514
More worlds slid by, but Zann was unable to reach any of them.

24
00:01:51.515 --> 00:01:59.920
It was a struggle merely staying conscious and alert; with every passing moment, he could feel more energy draining from him.

25
00:01:59.921 --> 00:02:05.767
Soon he felt as if even a simple Door-opening spell would be more than he could manage.

26
00:02:05.768 --> 00:02:09.685
Would he and his friends end up spinning through the vortex forever?

27
00:02:09.686 --> 00:02:15.562
Like Morb, like poor Venna under the Dousing spell, like Zann's parents?

28
00:02:15.563 --> 00:02:18.879
"We have to do something!" Perda cried.

29
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:26.992
"I know." Even pushing out the words took almost more energy than Zann had left. "I just don't—"

30
00:02:26.993 --> 00:02:30.467
Suddenly Zing whistled eagerly in his ear.

31
00:02:30.468 --> 00:02:36.966
Another wormhole was sliding past; this one revealed a large fish leaping out of the water.

32
00:02:36.967 --> 00:02:43.278
Zing lunged, stretching out with his front claws while keeping his hind claws in Zann's backpack.

33
00:02:43.279 --> 00:02:47.751
"Zing!" Darb cried. "This is no time to think about food!"

34
00:02:47.752 --> 00:02:51.849
But somehow Zing was clawing at the edge of the wormhole.

35
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:58.187
Zann felt a strong sucking sensation, as if his entire body were being compressed.

36
00:02:58.188 --> 00:03:02.821
"Wait!" Gliss cried. "I'm losing hold of Perda—"

37
00:03:02.822 --> 00:03:04.306
Splash

38
00:03:04.307 --> 00:03:10.989
! Zann plunged into a gray sea. Its waves grabbed him, flipping him head over

39
00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:14.939
heels. It was almost as disorienting as being in the

40
00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:19.400
vortex. Zann was so tired that he wasn't sure he could fight the angry water.

41
00:03:19.401 --> 00:03:23.879
He was tempted to give up, let himself sink beneath the waves forever . . .

42
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.548
Then he felt a yank on his arm.

43
00:03:26.549 --> 00:03:32.437
A moment later his head popped above the surface and he gulped in cool, moist air.

44
00:03:32.438 --> 00:03:36.409
Perda was bobbing beside him, panting with exhaustion.

45
00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:39.886
"Where's everyone else?" she asked.

46
00:03:39.887 --> 00:03:44.641
Wind-driven rain made it hard to see. Zann blinked away the moisture.

47
00:03:44.642 --> 00:03:49.356
Zing was floating nearby, flapping his wings and looking disgusted.

48
00:03:49.357 --> 00:03:53.489
Zann almost smiled. The dragon wasn't a fan of swimming.

49
00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:57.315
One of Zann's favorite tricks was to dunk him in the river.

50
00:03:57.316 --> 00:04:01.769
Zann tried to focus; he realized his weary mind was wandering.

51
00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:07.567
Treading water, he turned and spotted Gliss and Darb bobbing nearby.

52
00:04:07.568 --> 00:04:09.943
"There you are!" he called.

53
00:04:09.944 --> 00:04:15.153
He struck out toward them but realized his arm was still attached to Perda's.

54
00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:22.035
For a moment he was annoyed. Then he realized that the shackles were what had saved him.

55
00:04:22.036 --> 00:04:24.316
She must have pulled him to the surface.

56
00:04:24.317 --> 00:04:33.373
By now Darb and Gliss had spotted them and were swimming over. "Everyone okay?" Darb panted.

57
00:04:33.374 --> 00:04:39.277
"I think so." Zann squeezed his eyes shut as a larger wave washed over them.

58
00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:43.510
He was relieved to feel his magic energy already coming back.

59
00:04:43.511 --> 00:04:47.832
He glanced at Zing, who had finally shaken off enough water to fly.

60
00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:54.773
"Go higher, boy!" Zann called. "Find land!" He glanced at the others.

61
00:04:54.774 --> 00:05:01.646
"Try to rest. Then when Zing shows us which direction to go, we can zap to land."

62
00:05:01.647 --> 00:05:06.085
"Yeah," Gliss said. " If our magic works in this

63
00:05:06.086 --> 00:05:09.241
world." Zann gulped. He hadn't thought of

64
00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:13.910
that. "I'll test my magic." Perda touched the shackles.

65
00:05:13.911 --> 00:05:18.741
"Release!" The shackles disappeared. "Looks like it still works," Zann

66
00:05:18.742 --> 00:05:22.565
said. "It's weird here," Gliss said, her voice

67
00:05:22.566 --> 00:05:27.843
shaking. "The rain—it's not any color at all! Just

68
00:05:27.844 --> 00:05:33.082
clear!" "Never mind that," Perda said. "I'm getting tired. Let's make a boat or

69
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:35.745
something." She linked hands with Zann and

70
00:05:35.746 --> 00:05:41.552
Gliss. Even combined, their energy was weak. All they could manage was a small wooden

71
00:05:41.553 --> 00:05:44.963
raft. When it was finished, Zann felt drained once

72
00:05:44.964 --> 00:05:48.654
again. Still, the raft was big enough to hold them

73
00:05:48.655 --> 00:05:58.178
all. "What's taking him so long?" Gliss squinted up at Zing, who was circling rapidly overhead. The dragon's whistle sounded

74
00:05:58.179 --> 00:06:03.893
uneasy. Suddenly Zing squawked loudly and dived toward them. Zann

75
00:06:03.894 --> 00:06:06.662
frowned. "What's he doing?" he

76
00:06:06.663 --> 00:06:11.646
wondered. At that moment something jolted the raft from below, flipping it up and

77
00:06:11.647 --> 00:06:16.705
over. Zann barely had time to gasp before he felt himself falling into the

78
00:06:16.706 --> 00:06:25.155
sea. He fought his way back to the surface just in time to see their raft being swallowed by a creature like none he'd ever seen

79
00:06:25.156 --> 00:06:35.474
before. It was a huge, jelly-like beast the size of the largest dragons—like an enormous jellyfish with a gaping, hungry mouth.

80
00:06:35.475 --> 00:07:04.733
And several more were surfacing nearby!

